1
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:16,360
This is the fourth video presentation for the Case Animal and Plant Biotechnology course.
这是 CASE 动植物生物技术课程的第四个视频演示。

2
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:20,860
As you view this video, be sure to make notes of important information.
观看本视频时，请务必记下重要信息。

3
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:25,060
Feel free to pause, repeat, and resume the video whenever necessary.
必要时可以随时暂停、重播和继续播放视频。

4
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:30,560
Peer Reviews Lesson 4.1, Genetically Modified Organisms
同伴评审，第 4.1 课，转基因生物

5
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:38,360
As steps in the process of writing a research paper for Project 2.2.4, Rooted in Research,
作为为项目 2.2.4“扎根研究”撰写研究论文过程中的步骤，

6
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:41,860
you have completed an annotated bibliography and a rough draft.
你已经完成了一份带注释的参考文献目录和一份草稿。

7
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:47,860
This presentation provides information about how to properly review a peer's rough draft
本演示介绍如何正确评审同伴的草稿，

8
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:53,360
and provide helpful feedback to improve the content, organization, and flow.
并提供有用的反馈，以改进内容、结构和行文流畅度。

9
00:00:55,550 --> 00:01:01,050
Before you read the paper, review the Project 2.2.4 Evaluation Rubric.
在阅读论文之前，先复习项目 2.2.4 的评分标准。

10
00:01:01,550 --> 00:01:06,550
During the first read, make notes of any items you feel need further attention.
第一遍阅读时，记下你认为需要进一步注意的任何地方。

11
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:10,550
Include suggestions for improvement as well as pointing out strengths.
既要提出改进建议，也要指出优点。

12
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:24,380
The basic feedback to provide will help the writer improve content, organization, grammar, mechanics, effect, and formatting.
要提供的基本反馈将帮助作者改进内容、结构、语法、写作规范、表达效果和格式。

13
00:01:28,910 --> 00:01:32,910
Use this list of questions to help you evaluate the paper's content.
用这份问题清单来帮助你评估论文的内容。

14
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:39,410
The content must be related to the thesis and sources must substantiate claims made throughout the paper.
内容必须与论点相关，而且资料来源必须能够证实论文中提出的各项观点。

15
00:01:39,410 --> 00:01:46,740
Appraise the paper's organization with the next six points.
用接下来的六点来评价论文的结构。

16
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:49,740
The thesis is a critical first impression.
论点是至关重要的第一印象。

17
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:54,240
A clear thesis dictates focus and main points of the paper.
一个清晰的论点决定了论文的重点和要点。

18
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:05,540
A well-organized paper will have a logical flow, ideas to substantiate the thesis, and an appropriate focus.
一篇结构良好的论文会有合乎逻辑的行文、支撑论点的观点以及恰当的重点。

19
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:14,830
During the introduction, the author should establish the thesis and the direction of the paper's contents.
在引言中，作者应确立论点和论文内容的方向。

20
00:02:14,830 --> 00:02:24,690
The body of the paper should provide multiple focused points with facts to verify the thesis statement.
论文正文应提供多个重点明确的论点，并用事实来验证论点陈述。

21
00:02:25,190 --> 00:02:34,020
To affirm the thesis, the conclusion will complete the paper in a concise manner.
为了肯定论点，结论部分应以简洁的方式完结全文。

22
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:45,700
Correctly used citations remove doubts about plagiarism in order to illustrate academic honesty.
正确使用引注可以消除对剽窃的疑虑，从而体现学术诚信。

23
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:50,700
Citations also provide details about from where information originated.
引注还提供了信息来源的详细情况。

24
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:57,540
Cited references must have complete entries included in a list of references.
被引用的参考资料必须在参考文献列表中列出完整条目。

25
00:02:58,040 --> 00:03:01,540
References must follow APA citation format.
参考文献必须遵循 APA 引用格式。

26
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:10,630
Proper grammar and mechanics improve the readability of a paper.
正确的语法和写作规范能提高论文的可读性。

27
00:03:11,130 --> 00:03:16,630
Errors can be distracting for the reader or even change the intent of a sentence.
错误会分散读者的注意力，甚至改变句子的本意。

28
00:03:17,130 --> 00:03:24,890
Consistent formatting will also improve the ease of reading.
统一的格式也会让阅读更加轻松。

29
00:03:24,890 --> 00:03:31,230
Content alone is not enough, though.
不过，光有内容是不够的。

30
00:03:31,730 --> 00:03:37,230
Well-crafted sentences and phrases effectively communicate the true intent of the paper.
精心组织的句子和措辞能有效地传达论文的真正意图。

31
00:03:37,730 --> 00:03:41,230
The paper should, on the whole, maintain reader interest.
论文总体上应能保持读者的兴趣。

32
00:03:41,730 --> 00:03:47,460
Be sure to point out what is done well.
一定要指出哪些地方做得好。

33
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:52,460
Include suggestions for improvements rather than simply point out the problems.
要提出改进建议，而不只是简单地指出问题。

34
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:56,460
Ask questions to clarify confusing passages.
对令人困惑的段落提出问题，以便澄清。

35
00:03:56,460 --> 00:04:08,180
As a review, mark or highlight key points in your notes that are important to remember from this presentation.
作为复习，请在笔记中标记或突出显示本演示中需要记住的要点。

36
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:13,180
List two ideas or concepts that relate to previous knowledge.
列出两个与已有知识相关的观点或概念。

37
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:16,180
List any questions you have about this topic.
列出你对这个主题的任何疑问。

38
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:19,180
Discuss these questions with your instructor.
与你的老师讨论这些问题。

39
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:25,180
Keep any notes you have from this presentation organized and available for use throughout the course.
把你在本演示中做的所有笔记整理好，以便在整个课程中随时使用。

40
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:31,680
Through the peer review process, you will improve your critical reading and feedback skills.
通过同伴评审过程，你将提高批判性阅读和反馈能力。

41
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:34,680
Your teacher will provide more instructions.
你的老师会提供更多说明。
